1
00:00:01,910 --> 00:00:05,510
So you are considering going into experimental physics,

2
00:00:05,510 --> 00:00:07,270
My door is always open.

3
00:00:07,270 --> 00:00:10,310
Once again, I'm sorry that the demonstration didn't quite work out,

4
00:00:10,310 --> 00:00:13,070
But now we know what happens when you accidentally spill

5
00:00:13,070 --> 00:00:16,760
Peach snapple into a helium neon laser.

6
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:20,210
Short answer is... don't.

7
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:27,470
And now to tell you about the theoretical physics department

8
00:00:27,470 --> 00:00:29,140
Is dr. sheldon cooper.

9
00:00:33,410 --> 00:00:34,410
Dr. cooper?

10
00:00:34,410 --> 00:00:36,570
Forget it.

11
00:00:36,570 --> 00:00:38,540
Excuse me.

12
00:00:40,070 --> 00:00:41,710
Sheldon, we both agreed to do this.

13
00:00:41,710 --> 00:00:42,940
It's a waste of time.

14
00:00:42,940 --> 00:00:45,010
I might as well explain the laws of thermodynamics

15
00:00:45,010 --> 00:00:46,370
To a bunch of labradoodles.

16
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:52,740
If you don't do this, i won't take you to the comic book store.

17
00:00:55,010 --> 00:00:56,840
Hello.

18
00:00:59,910 --> 00:01:03,710
Nice work with the laser, by the way.

19
00:01:04,970 --> 00:01:08,770
Looking out at your fresh young faces,

20
00:01:08,770 --> 00:01:12,070
I remember when I too was deciding my academic future

21
00:01:12,070 --> 00:01:15,210
As a lowly graduate student.

22
00:01:15,210 --> 00:01:17,670
Of course, I was 14.

23
00:01:17,670 --> 00:01:19,670
And I'd already achieved more than most of you

24
00:01:19,670 --> 00:01:23,040
Could ever hope to, despite my 9:00 bedtime.

25
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:27,270
Now, there may be one or two of you in this room

26
00:01:27,270 --> 00:01:30,440
Who has what it takes to succeed in theoretical physics.

27
00:01:30,440 --> 00:01:32,440
Although, it's more likely that you'll spend

28
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:34,310
Your scientific careers teaching fifth graders

29
00:01:34,310 --> 00:01:36,120
How to make papier mache volcanoes

30
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:37,940
with baking soda lava.

31
00:01:39,370 --> 00:01:40,450
Oh, good god.

32
00:01:40,450 --> 00:01:41,540
In short--

33
00:01:41,540 --> 00:01:44,370
Any one who told you that you would someday be able

34
00:01:44,370 --> 00:01:46,540
To make any significant contribution to physics,

35
00:01:46,540 --> 00:01:49,740
Played a cruel trick on you, a cruel trick indeed.

36
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:53,670
Any questions?

37
00:01:56,340 --> 00:01:59,710
Of course not.

38
00:01:59,710 --> 00:02:01,770
I weep for the future of science.

39
00:02:01,770 --> 00:02:04,560
Now if you'll excuse me, the latest issue of batman is out.

40
00:02:05,310 --> 00:02:07,310
Come, leonard.

41
00:02:10,070 --> 00:02:14,170
Laser demonstration's looking pretty good now, huh?

42
00:02:39,150 --> 00:02:40,390
I love this time of the year.

43
00:02:40,390 --> 00:02:43,420
The leaves are turning, there's a bracing chill in the air.

44
00:02:43,420 --> 00:02:46,290
Plus there's a whole new crop of female grad students

45
00:02:46,290 --> 00:02:48,320
About to put on just enough winter weight

46
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:50,490
To make them needy and vulnerable.

47
00:02:51,950 --> 00:02:54,750
That's right, honey, have another calzone.

48
00:02:54,750 --> 00:02:56,450
Daddy can wait.

49
00:02:58,620 --> 00:03:01,590
Isn't there a university policy against dating graduate students?

50
00:03:01,590 --> 00:03:03,590
No, if you can talk to them, you can ask them out.

51
00:03:03,590 --> 00:03:05,990
Damn, there's always a catch.

52
00:03:07,090 --> 00:03:08,090
Hey, guys.

53
00:03:08,090 --> 00:03:09,090
Hey, leslie.

54
00:03:09,090 --> 00:03:12,620
So, dumbass, I heard you made a grad student throw up last night.

55
00:03:12,620 --> 00:03:16,230
The truth can indeed be a finger down the throat

56
00:03:16,230 --> 00:03:17,610
Of those unprepared to hear it.

57
00:03:17,890 --> 00:03:21,050
But why should I cater to second-rate minds?

58
00:03:21,050 --> 00:03:25,020
Because first-rate minds call you "dumbass"?

59
00:03:26,450 --> 00:03:28,320
Oh, yeah? well...

60
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:30,850
You're a mean person.

61
00:03:31,850 --> 00:03:33,250
Excuse me, dr. cooper,

62
00:03:33,250 --> 00:03:34,350
I'm ramona nowitzki.

63
00:03:34,350 --> 00:03:36,090
I was at your talk last night.

64
00:03:36,090 --> 00:03:38,150
I think you're just brilliant.

65
00:03:38,150 --> 00:03:40,550
That is the prevailing opinion.

66
00:03:40,550 --> 00:03:43,850
Oh, now I'm gonna throw up.

67
00:03:43,850 --> 00:03:46,420
Howard wolowitz, department of engineering,

68
00:03:46,420 --> 00:03:51,320
Co-designer of the international space station's liquid waste disposal system.

69
00:03:52,850 --> 00:03:54,650
Ew.

70
00:03:57,920 --> 00:04:00,420
Dr. cooper, I've read everything you've published.

71
00:04:00,420 --> 00:04:02,790
I especially liked your paper on grand unification

72
00:04:02,790 --> 00:04:04,190
Using string-network condensates

73
00:04:04,190 --> 00:04:05,450
And were wondering how you determined

74
00:04:05,450 --> 00:04:06,820
That three-dimensional string-nets provided

75
00:04:06,820 --> 00:04:09,920
A unified picture of fermions and gauge bosons?

76
00:04:09,920 --> 00:04:14,390
Amazing, an intelligent labradoodle.

77
00:04:14,390 --> 00:04:17,150
Woof.

78
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:20,650
The fact is I'm quite close to a breakthrough

79
00:04:20,650 --> 00:04:23,350
In showing how neutrinos emerge from a string-net condensate.

80
00:04:23,350 --> 00:04:26,620
Oh, my god, that would change the way we view the entire physical universe.

81
00:04:26,620 --> 00:04:29,390
It's what I do.

82
00:04:29,390 --> 00:04:32,620
You know, the pishkin-wolowitz liquid waste disposal system

83
00:04:32,620 --> 00:04:35,820
Is turning a few heads as well.

84
00:04:39,220 --> 00:04:41,820
Again, ew.

85
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:46,620
You know, I'd love to hear more about how you intend to add neutrinos.

86
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:48,850
Could we get a cup of coffee sometime?

87
00:04:48,850 --> 00:04:50,450
I don't drink coffee.

88
00:04:50,450 --> 00:04:52,490
I do. I love me a cup of joe.

89
00:04:52,490 --> 00:04:54,250
Well, it doesn't have to be coffee.

90
00:04:54,250 --> 00:04:55,390
How about dinner?

91
00:04:55,390 --> 00:04:57,020
I do eat dinner.

92
00:04:57,020 --> 00:04:58,550
Great. I know a terrific little italian place.

93
00:04:58,550 --> 00:05:00,250
I never eat in strange restaurants.

94
00:05:00,250 --> 00:05:02,890
One runs the risk of non-standard cutlery.

95
00:05:02,890 --> 00:05:04,850
Excuse me?

96
00:05:04,850 --> 00:05:08,920
Sheldon lives in fear of the three-tined fork.

97
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:10,720
Three tines is not a fork.

98
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:12,450
Three tines is a trident.

99
00:05:12,450 --> 00:05:13,690
Forks are for eating,

100
00:05:13,690 --> 00:05:17,290
Tridents are for ruling the seven seas.

101
00:05:17,290 --> 00:05:19,250
What if I brought food to your place?

102
00:05:19,250 --> 00:05:21,020
That would be acceptable.

103
00:05:21,020 --> 00:05:22,950
On mondays, I eat thai food.

104
00:05:22,950 --> 00:05:24,720
Mee krob and chicken sate

105
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:26,820
With extra peanut sauce from siam palace.

106
00:05:26,820 --> 00:05:28,050
You got it.

107
00:05:28,050 --> 00:05:30,120
I already have your address.

108
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:35,620
What a nice girl.

109
00:05:35,620 --> 00:05:38,750
Sheldon, do you have any idea what just happened?

110
00:05:38,750 --> 00:05:42,550
Yes. apparently I'm getting a free dinner.

111
00:05:46,790 --> 00:05:49,920
Oh, yeah, no, this thing's majorly out of order.

112
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:51,520
- See? - sorry.

113
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:52,720
That's okay.

114
00:05:52,720 --> 00:05:54,190
Guess I'm taking the stairs.

115
00:05:54,190 --> 00:05:55,290
Where you going?

116
00:05:55,290 --> 00:05:56,450
4-a.

117
00:05:56,450 --> 00:05:57,790
Oh, are you here to see leonard?

118
00:05:57,790 --> 00:05:59,620
No, dr. cooper.

119
00:05:59,620 --> 00:06:02,620
Dr. sheldon cooper?

120
00:06:02,620 --> 00:06:04,350
We're having dinner.

121
00:06:04,350 --> 00:06:06,620
Sheldon cooper?

122
00:06:08,050 --> 00:06:09,390
Tall, thin,

123
00:06:09,390 --> 00:06:13,720
Looks a little like a giant praying mantis?

124
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:17,020
He is cute, isn't he?

125
00:06:19,290 --> 00:06:21,420
Sheldon cooper?

126
00:06:24,520 --> 00:06:25,690
Hi, leonard.

127
00:06:25,690 --> 00:06:26,950
Hey, ramona. come on in.

128
00:06:26,950 --> 00:06:28,620
Thanks. where should I put this?

129
00:06:28,620 --> 00:06:30,020
Uh, the kitchen's fine.

130
00:06:30,020 --> 00:06:31,150
Hey, what are you doing?

131
00:06:31,150 --> 00:06:33,750
I need to see this. uh-huh.

132
00:06:33,750 --> 00:06:36,690
The viewing area's right over there.

133
00:06:40,020 --> 00:06:43,320
Sheldon, your girl... date... person... ramona's here.

134
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:45,690
Oh, hello.

135
00:06:45,690 --> 00:06:47,150
Oh, sorry I'm late.

136
00:06:47,150 --> 00:06:49,550
I just got so caught up reading the draft of your latest paper.

137
00:06:49,550 --> 00:06:51,450
Did you enjoy the humorous footnote

138
00:06:51,450 --> 00:06:52,890
Where I illustrate  mirror-symmetry

139
00:06:52,890 --> 00:06:55,290
By likening it to the flash playing tennis with himself?

140
00:06:55,290 --> 00:06:56,990
So funny.

141
00:06:58,490 --> 00:07:01,020
But the idea that you might be able to incorporate gravity,

142
00:07:01,020 --> 00:07:05,820
I have to tell you, I found it  physically exhilarating.

143
00:07:05,820 --> 00:07:09,050
My hypotheses tend to have that effect.

144
00:07:10,790 --> 00:07:12,320
I'm sorry I didn't bring enough For your friends.

145
00:07:13,550 --> 00:07:15,990
I assumed we were going to be alone.

146
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:21,150
No, we were just going.

147
00:07:21,150 --> 00:07:22,750
To watch, right?

148
00:07:22,750 --> 00:07:26,450
No, come on, now, we're going out.

149
00:07:26,450 --> 00:07:28,990
Oh, come on, we'll be quiet.

150
00:07:28,990 --> 00:07:30,690
Let's go, let's go.

151
00:07:32,020 --> 00:07:33,350
Okay, you two.

152
00:07:33,350 --> 00:07:36,050
Have a nice...

153
00:07:36,050 --> 00:07:38,590
Whatever this is.

154
00:07:41,520 --> 00:07:44,290
Okay, you guys, look, i know this is none of my business,

155
00:07:44,290 --> 00:07:45,950
But I just... I have to ask--

156
00:07:45,950 --> 00:07:48,190
What's sheldon's deal?

157
00:07:50,390 --> 00:07:52,790
What do you mean "deal"?

158
00:07:52,790 --> 00:07:54,790
You know, like what's his deal?

159
00:07:54,790 --> 00:07:58,450
Is it girls...? guys...? sock puppets...?

160
00:07:58,450 --> 00:08:00,920
Honestly, we've been operating under the assumption

161
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:03,220
That he has no deal.

162
00:08:03,220 --> 00:08:05,220
Come on, everybody has a deal.

163
00:08:05,220 --> 00:08:06,520
Not sheldon.

164
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:08,520
Over the years, we've formulated many theories

165
00:08:08,520 --> 00:08:10,950
About how he might reproduce.

166
00:08:11,820 --> 00:08:15,320
I'm an advocate of mitosis.

167
00:08:15,320 --> 00:08:17,150
I'm sorry?

168
00:08:17,150 --> 00:08:19,990
I believe one day sheldon will eat an enormous amount

169
00:08:19,990 --> 00:08:24,220
Of thai food and split into two sheldons.

170
00:08:25,690 --> 00:08:27,190
On the other hand, I think sheldon

171
00:08:27,190 --> 00:08:29,020
Might be the larval form of his species,

172
00:08:29,020 --> 00:08:31,290
And someday he'll spin a cocoon and emerge two months later

173
00:08:31,290 --> 00:08:33,650
With moth wings and an exoskeleton.

174
00:08:33,650 --> 00:08:37,820
Okay, well, thanks for the nightmares.

175
00:08:37,820 --> 00:08:41,390
Hey, do you want to hang out with us?

176
00:08:41,390 --> 00:08:43,250
What are you guys gonna do?

177
00:08:45,690 --> 00:08:47,850
My mom's making a brisket tonight.

178
00:08:47,850 --> 00:08:53,650
The one with the little onions? mm...

179
00:08:53,650 --> 00:08:57,920
Yeah, I'm busy, so...

180
00:08:57,920 --> 00:08:59,790
Good night.

181
00:08:59,790 --> 00:09:02,820
Her loss. let's go.

182
00:09:02,820 --> 00:09:04,750
Brisket party!

183
00:09:04,750 --> 00:09:07,090
B-to-the-r-to-the-i-s-k...

184
00:09:07,920 --> 00:09:10,490
To-the-e-to-the-t...

185
00:09:18,860 --> 00:09:20,160
Hey, aren't you having breakfast?

186
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:22,660
Yes.

187
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:26,820
Are you experimenting with nutritional suppositories again?

188
00:09:26,820 --> 00:09:30,390
Not in these pants.

189
00:09:30,390 --> 00:09:34,360
So... how'd it go with ramona last night?

190
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:38,060
Oh, great. She's smart, insightful

191
00:09:38,060 --> 00:09:42,220
And she has a very unique way of, you know, revering me.

192
00:09:43,360 --> 00:09:46,000
Here's your spinach mushroom omelet .

193
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:48,400
Thank you.

194
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:50,030
Did anyone touch it?

195
00:09:50,030 --> 00:09:53,300
Gloves were worn by everyone involved. I was vigilant.

196
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:56,830
Ramona pointed out that I've been wasting 20 minutes a day

197
00:09:56,830 --> 00:09:58,900
Standing on cafeteria lines.

198
00:09:58,900 --> 00:10:00,330
Time which would be better spent

199
00:10:00,330 --> 00:10:02,200
Tackling the great physics problems of our day.

200
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:04,060
You don't tackle the big issues, ramona.

201
00:10:04,060 --> 00:10:05,060
You fence with them.

202
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:08,460
En garde. riposte.

203
00:10:11,400 --> 00:10:13,400
Touche.

204
00:10:14,660 --> 00:10:16,090
Morning.

205
00:10:16,090 --> 00:10:17,260
Hi, leslie.

206
00:10:17,260 --> 00:10:18,360
So, sheldon,

207
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:23,290
I see you're organizing your papers for the smithsonian museum of dumbassery.

208
00:10:23,290 --> 00:10:25,160
There won't be any room

209
00:10:25,160 --> 00:10:28,590
Until they get rid of the permanent leslie winkle exhibit.

210
00:10:29,990 --> 00:10:31,490
Oh, good one.

211
00:10:31,490 --> 00:10:34,990
I see you got a grad student to fight your battles for you.

212
00:10:34,990 --> 00:10:37,520
I'll let you keep your lunch money today.

213
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:40,420
Okay, dr. cooper is on the verge of a breakthrough.

214
00:10:40,420 --> 00:10:41,490
If you're going to stay,

215
00:10:41,490 --> 00:10:44,390
You'll have to be respectful and quiet.

216
00:10:52,090 --> 00:10:53,360
Wait for me.

217
00:10:56,820 --> 00:10:59,690
So have you worked out the neutrino issue?

218
00:10:59,690 --> 00:11:01,890
Well, to paraphrase mozart,

219
00:11:01,890 --> 00:11:03,390
All the subatomic particles are there.

220
00:11:03,390 --> 00:11:05,560
I just have to put them in the right order.

221
00:11:05,560 --> 00:11:06,860
You're so witty.

222
00:11:06,860 --> 00:11:08,920
Aren't i?

223
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:15,960
Hey, guys, this package came for...

224
00:11:19,890 --> 00:11:21,560
Dr. cooper is working.

225
00:11:21,560 --> 00:11:23,890
Yes, I'm close to a breakthrough.

226
00:11:23,890 --> 00:11:25,220
Ooh, it tickles!

227
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:28,190
Sorry.

228
00:11:32,620 --> 00:11:35,760
Holy crap on a cracker.

229
00:11:35,760 --> 00:11:37,890
Hey, penny.

230
00:11:37,890 --> 00:11:40,090
Hi. you probably don't want to go in there.

231
00:11:40,090 --> 00:11:41,590
Why? what are they doing?

232
00:11:41,590 --> 00:11:44,290
The only way I could explain it

233
00:11:44,290 --> 00:11:46,920
Would be in a therapist's office with dolls.

234
00:11:55,420 --> 00:11:57,990
Hoo-boy.

235
00:11:57,990 --> 00:12:00,790
Dr. cooper's working.

236
00:12:00,790 --> 00:12:02,990
Yeah, I can see that.

237
00:12:02,990 --> 00:12:06,120
Sheldon, halo night, koothrappali's. you coming?

238
00:12:06,120 --> 00:12:08,590
Oh, yes, it's halo night.

239
00:12:08,590 --> 00:12:10,320
Let me just dry my tootsies.

240
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:12,620
You're not going to halo night.

241
00:12:12,620 --> 00:12:13,820
Yes, I am.

242
00:12:13,820 --> 00:12:16,820
It's wednesday. wednesday's halo night.

243
00:12:16,820 --> 00:12:20,420
Didn't a great man once say, "science demands nothing less

244
00:12:20,420 --> 00:12:24,060
"than the fervent and unconditional dedication of our entire lives"?

245
00:12:24,060 --> 00:12:25,660
He did.

246
00:12:25,660 --> 00:12:27,420
And who was that great man?

247
00:12:27,420 --> 00:12:30,190
Me.

248
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:32,790
Sorry, leonard.

249
00:12:32,790 --> 00:12:34,320
Seriously? you're not coming?

250
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:37,960
You heard her. how can I argue with me?

251
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:42,590
Okay, well, once again, you guys have a good...

252
00:12:42,590 --> 00:12:44,820
Whatever this is.

253
00:12:46,690 --> 00:12:48,860
Dr. cooper, I have to tell you

254
00:12:48,860 --> 00:12:50,520
Your friends are holding you back.

255
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:53,960
I prefer to think of it as "i'm pulling them forward."

256
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:56,820
Halo night?

257
00:12:56,820 --> 00:12:58,060
A man with your intellectual gifts

258
00:12:58,060 --> 00:13:00,720
Doesn't waste an evening playing video games.

259
00:13:00,720 --> 00:13:03,220
He does on wednesdays.

260
00:13:03,220 --> 00:13:05,590
Not if he wants a nobel prize.

261
00:13:05,590 --> 00:13:09,420
He does want that.

262
00:13:09,420 --> 00:13:12,320
Does a man with my intellectual gifts

263
00:13:12,320 --> 00:13:13,520
Play paintball on weekends?

264
00:13:13,520 --> 00:13:15,220
What do you think?

265
00:13:15,220 --> 00:13:17,260
Drat.

266
00:13:17,260 --> 00:13:20,190
Now shall we get back to work?

267
00:13:20,190 --> 00:13:22,860
I suppose.

268
00:13:25,860 --> 00:13:27,720
Battlestar galactica  comes on tonight.

269
00:13:28,490 --> 00:13:30,760
I guess I can wait for the dvd.

270
00:13:31,820 --> 00:13:35,260
And then never ever watch it.

271
00:14:33,560 --> 00:14:35,690
Penny! penny!

272
00:14:35,690 --> 00:14:37,090
Penny!

273
00:14:37,090 --> 00:14:38,560
Sheldon, honey, I've told you,

274
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:39,720
It's a small apartment.

275
00:14:39,720 --> 00:14:41,190
You only have to knock one time.

276
00:14:41,190 --> 00:14:43,360
Please, please, I don't have a lot of time.

277
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:44,420
Look, ramona finally dozed off,

278
00:14:44,420 --> 00:14:47,120
And I need you to help me get rid of her.

279
00:14:49,120 --> 00:14:50,960
Get rid of her how?

280
00:14:50,960 --> 00:14:52,260
I don't know,

281
00:14:52,260 --> 00:14:54,390
But apparently I'm in some kind of relationship,

282
00:14:54,390 --> 00:14:58,460
And you seem to be an expert at ending them.

283
00:15:01,890 --> 00:15:03,320
Excuse me?

284
00:15:03,320 --> 00:15:06,920
I see man after man leaving this apartment never to return.

285
00:15:06,920 --> 00:15:11,190
Okay, first of all, it is not man after man.

286
00:15:11,190 --> 00:15:13,260
Dr. cooper?! hide me.

287
00:15:13,260 --> 00:15:15,390
Hide you?

288
00:15:15,390 --> 00:15:17,520
I formally request sanctuary.

289
00:15:18,390 --> 00:15:20,260
Why aren't you working?

290
00:15:22,290 --> 00:15:23,960
She distracted me.

291
00:15:25,190 --> 00:15:27,790
I told you, penny, I don't have time for your nonsense.

292
00:15:27,790 --> 00:15:29,890
I have important things to do.

293
00:15:32,620 --> 00:15:34,220
Oh, man.

294
00:15:34,220 --> 00:15:35,520
I know what's going on here.

295
00:15:35,520 --> 00:15:36,560
Really?

296
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:38,620
Well, then will you explain it to me?

297
00:15:38,620 --> 00:15:40,890
You're in love with dr. cooper.

298
00:15:40,890 --> 00:15:44,660
Uh, yeah, no, that's not it.

299
00:15:44,660 --> 00:15:46,420
Don't try to deny it.

300
00:15:46,420 --> 00:15:48,220
He's a remarkable man,

301
00:15:48,220 --> 00:15:50,990
But you have to let him go.

302
00:15:50,990 --> 00:15:53,860
Oh, gee, okay.

303
00:15:53,860 --> 00:15:56,960
I know it's hard, but he's a gift to the whole world,

304
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:58,490
And we can't be selfish.

305
00:15:58,490 --> 00:16:01,660
Yeah, he's a gift all right.

306
00:16:01,660 --> 00:16:04,520
Sisters?

307
00:16:06,090 --> 00:16:07,860
Uh, sure.

308
00:16:07,860 --> 00:16:09,620
Sisters.

309
00:16:13,620 --> 00:16:16,920
Holy crap on a cracker.

310
00:16:23,620 --> 00:16:26,290
Sheldon?

311
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:34,490
What are you doing?!

312
00:16:34,490 --> 00:16:36,160
It's morse code.

313
00:16:36,160 --> 00:16:38,660
Why?

314
00:16:38,660 --> 00:16:41,260
So we can communicate through the wall.

315
00:16:41,260 --> 00:16:45,220
We are communicating through the wall.

316
00:16:45,220 --> 00:16:49,360
Yes, but the communication is not encrypted.

317
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:51,220
I don't know morse code.

318
00:16:51,220 --> 00:16:52,160
It's very simple.

319
00:16:52,160 --> 00:16:55,490
This is a ... This is b ... this is c...

320
00:16:55,490 --> 00:16:59,020
Sheldon, I'm not going to learn morse code at 3:00 in the morning!

321
00:16:59,020 --> 00:17:01,520
All right.

322
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:04,520
Don't come in here, don't come in here, don't come in here,

323
00:17:04,520 --> 00:17:07,560
Don't... oh!

324
00:17:09,060 --> 00:17:10,090
What's going on?

325
00:17:10,090 --> 00:17:12,620
Shh! ramona's sleeping on the couch.

326
00:17:12,620 --> 00:17:14,520
I know. when is she going home?

327
00:17:14,520 --> 00:17:17,060
Never. that's the problem.

328
00:17:17,060 --> 00:17:18,290
I need your help.

329
00:17:18,290 --> 00:17:19,960
What are you talking about?

330
00:17:19,960 --> 00:17:24,120
I'm invoking the skynet clause of our friendship agreement.

331
00:17:24,120 --> 00:17:26,090
That only applies if you need me

332
00:17:26,090 --> 00:17:27,890
To help you destroy an artificial intelligence

333
00:17:27,890 --> 00:17:30,660
You've created that's taking over the earth.

334
00:17:30,660 --> 00:17:32,020
Come on! don't nitpick!

335
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:35,990
Good night.

336
00:17:35,990 --> 00:17:38,490
Shh. all right.

337
00:17:38,490 --> 00:17:41,060
I'm invoking our body snatchers clause.

338
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:43,090
The body snatchers clause requires me

339
00:17:43,090 --> 00:17:44,890
To help you destroy someone we know

340
00:17:44,890 --> 00:17:47,090
Who's been replaced with an alien pod.

341
00:17:47,090 --> 00:17:48,720
Yes. she's in the living room. go.

342
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:49,790
I'll wait here.

343
00:17:49,790 --> 00:17:52,460
Sheldon, what are you doing out of bed?

344
00:17:52,460 --> 00:17:54,860
Now! do it!

345
00:17:56,660 --> 00:17:58,320
You know you need your sleep

346
00:17:58,320 --> 00:17:59,760
In order for your cognitive processing

347
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:01,790
To perform at optimum levels. now come on.

348
00:18:01,790 --> 00:18:03,760
Godzilla clause?

349
00:18:03,760 --> 00:18:06,860
Not unless she destroys tokyo.

350
00:18:06,860 --> 00:18:09,160
Rats.

351
00:18:10,360 --> 00:18:12,090
I've got it!

352
00:18:12,090 --> 00:18:14,690
I finally reconciled the black hole information paradox

353
00:18:14,690 --> 00:18:16,990
With my theory of string-network condensates!

354
00:18:16,990 --> 00:18:18,720
It's unbelievable!

355
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:20,420
It's paradigm-altering.

356
00:18:20,420 --> 00:18:22,260
And I could not have done it without you.

357
00:18:22,260 --> 00:18:24,520
Oh, please, I just offered a little encouragement.

358
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:26,020
It was a lot more than that.

359
00:18:26,020 --> 00:18:28,420
You helped me work out the masses of all the fermions

360
00:18:28,420 --> 00:18:30,490
And you pumiced my hammer toe.

361
00:18:32,120 --> 00:18:33,590
How can I ever repay you?

362
00:18:33,590 --> 00:18:37,260
Well, would you consider naming it the cooper-nowitzki theorem?

363
00:18:37,260 --> 00:18:39,590
Who's nowitzki?

364
00:18:39,590 --> 00:18:41,790
I'm nowitzki.

365
00:18:41,790 --> 00:18:44,090
Oh, you want me to share credit?

366
00:18:44,090 --> 00:18:45,060
Uh-huh.

367
00:18:45,060 --> 00:18:48,520
Get out!

368
00:18:49,690 --> 00:18:50,490
Oh, hey, hi.

369
00:18:50,490 --> 00:18:54,160
Oh, bite me!

370
00:18:54,160 --> 00:18:56,860
Sisters?

371
00:18:59,620 --> 00:19:01,860
Excuse me, dr. cooper.

372
00:19:01,860 --> 00:19:03,490
I'm kathy o'brien.

373
00:19:03,490 --> 00:19:04,820
I just finished reading your paper

374
00:19:04,820 --> 00:19:07,090
Reconciling the black hole information paradox

375
00:19:07,090 --> 00:19:09,420
With your theory of string- network condensates,

376
00:19:09,420 --> 00:19:11,260
And it just took my breath away.

377
00:19:11,260 --> 00:19:16,390
Maybe when I publish it, I'll include an inhaler.

378
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:22,090
Would you possibly have any time for me to pick your brain?

379
00:19:22,090 --> 00:19:24,560
Let's see. today's thursday.

380
00:19:24,560 --> 00:19:26,520
Thursday nights, I eat pizza from giacomo's.

381
00:19:26,520 --> 00:19:28,020
Sausage, mushrooms, light olives.

382
00:19:28,020 --> 00:19:30,060
Great. I'll bring it to your place.

383
00:19:30,060 --> 00:19:31,820
I have the address.

384
00:19:34,390 --> 00:19:36,790
What a nice girl.

385
00:19:37,720 --> 00:19:41,060
Sheldon, do you see what just happened here?

386
00:19:41,060 --> 00:19:44,660
Yes, I'm getting a free pizza.

387
00:19:46,720 --> 00:19:47,620
I'm on a roll.

388
00:19:52,960 --> 00:19:55,090
More pad thai, please.

389
00:19:55,090 --> 00:19:57,420
Sheldon, you've already had four servings.

390
00:19:57,420 --> 00:19:58,890
You might want to slow down a bit, buddy.

391
00:19:58,890 --> 00:20:02,090
Just one more bite.

392
00:20:09,560 --> 00:20:11,590
Sheldon?

393
00:20:11,590 --> 00:20:12,920
Sheldon, are you okay?

394
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:16,020
I'm just so... full.

395
00:20:27,060 --> 00:20:28,690
That's it. no more thai food.

